# React UI Conventions

## Components

- Single-file sections: `src/components/<name>.tsx` (kebab-case)
- Multi-file sections: `src/components/<name>/` only when multiple related files exist
- Export default from component files
- Use functional components with explicit TypeScript props

## Styling

- Prefer Tailwind utility classes — never use SCSS
- Use `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` for conditional/merged classes
- Use CSS modules (`.module.css`) only when Tailwind is impractical (e.g. complex keyframe animations)
- Use shadcn primitives from `@/components/ui/`
- Add new shadcn components: `vp dlx shadcn@latest add <name>`

## Animations

- Use `motion` from `motion/react` for section animations
- Keep animation props minimal; match existing patterns in hero/about-me

## 3D Globe

- Three.js logic stays in `world-map/globe-canvas.tsx` and `world-map/utils.ts`
- Lazy-load globe via `React.lazy` (see `world-map/index.tsx`)
- Do not import Three.js directly in section components

## Avoid

- SCSS files or `.scss` imports
- Inline styles unless necessary for dynamic values
- Single-file component folders (use `src/components/<name>.tsx` instead)
- PascalCase folder or file names
